NNAAMMEE
     ccoo — check out RCS revisions

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ccoo [--TTVV] [--dd_d_a_t_e] [--ff[_r_e_v]] [--II[_r_e_v]] [--kk_m_o_d_e] [--ll[_r_e_v]] [--MM[_r_e_v]]
        [--pp[_r_e_v]] [--qq[_r_e_v]] [--rr[_r_e_v]] [--ss_s_t_a_t_e] [--uu[_r_e_v]] [--ww[_u_s_e_r]]
        [--xx_s_u_f_f_i_x_e_s] [--zz_t_z] _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccoo program is used to check out revisions from RCS files.

     When a file is checked out, a copy is taken from the RCS repository, mi‐
     nus its RCS information, and placed in the current working directory.
     Files may be checked out as the most recent revision or according to a
     specific revision, using the --rr option.

     Files are checked out in one of two possible modes: unlocked (the de‐
     fault) or locked (using the --ll option).  In unlocked mode, any user may
     check out the file for reading.  If changes are to be made to a file
     though, it will have to be locked using the --ll option.  During this time,
     no other users may check out the file whilst it is locked.

     ccoo also supports keyword substitution – see the rcs(1) man page for more
     information.

     The following options are supported:

     --dd_d_a_t_e  Retrieve revision as of the latest revision no later than _d_a_t_e.

     --ff[_r_e_v]
             Force the overwriting of the working file.

     --II[_r_e_v]
             Interactive mode.

     --kk_m_o_d_e  Specify the keyword substitution mode.

     --ll[_r_e_v]
             The same as --rr, but also locks the revision.

     --MM[_r_e_v]
             Set the modification time of the file to the date of the re‐
             trieved revision.

     --pp[_r_e_v]
             Print the latest revision no later than _r_e_v to standard output.

     --qq[_r_e_v]
             Be quiet about reporting.

     --rr[_r_e_v]
             Retrieve the latest revision no later than _r_e_v.

     --ss_s_t_a_t_e
             Retrieve revision of the specified _s_t_a_t_e only.

     --TT      Preserve the modification time of RCS files.

     --uu[_r_e_v]
             The same as --rr, but also unlocks the retrieved revision if it was
             locked.

     --VV      Print RCS's version number.

     --ww[_u_s_e_r]
             Retrieve the latest revision which was checked in by the speci‐
             fied _u_s_e_r.  If the _u_s_e_r argument is omitted, the login of the
             user issuing the command is assumed.

     --xx_s_u_f_f_i_x_e_s
             Specifies the suffixes for RCS files.  Suffixes should be sepa‐
             rated by the ‘/’ character.

     --zz_t_z    Specify the date output format in keyword substitution, and the
             default time zone for _d_a_t_e used in the --dd option.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     RCSINIT  If set, this variable should contain a list of space-delimited
              options that are prepended to the argument list.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ccoo utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Retrieve the latest revision of file _f_o_o_._c and lock it for further edit‐
     ing:

           $ co -l foo.c

     Retrieve revision 1.5 of file _f_o_o_._c:

           $ co -r1.5 foo.c

